Subject: [PATCH] Honor the disableWorldTracking option in XrController.configure()

XrController declares a module-level `disableWorldTracking_` flag and checks it
in several places, but the public `configure()` entry point never assigns it
from its argument. As a result `XR8.XrController.configure({disableWorldTracking:
true})` is silently ignored.

With the flag stuck at its `false` default, tracking-controller.ts requires
world tracking unconditionally and rejects camera sessions on non-mobile
devices:

    [XR] Reality with camera on non-mobile devices requires disableWorldTracking

The open-source engine ships with SLAM removed, so world tracking is not
available at all and Image Tracking cannot run without this option. This patch
adds the missing option declaration and the assignment in `configure()`.

